    "body": "## Chat03 post-merge checkpoint: main/local CI PASS; hosted alpha remains BLOCKED\n\n- Live `main@b435e70eb88b87b3c3324ef2a2da14cdf473f229` confirmed as ordinary merge of PR #456 with source history for #449/#450/#451/#454; GitHub automatically marks all four ancestral PRs merged. No source PR re-merge or rewrite performed.\n- All **7/7 new-main check runs successful**. Explicit exact-main workflow runs: [Private Gameplay API](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40910189734), [Chat03 CAS SQL](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40910189755), [AI Forensics](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40910189650), [Pages build/deploy](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40910187084). These establish source/local Worker/D1 checks, **not hosted gameplay auth**. Pages publish is not gameplay Worker deployment.\n- **Read-only provider inventory:** accessible Cloudflare account has Workers subdomain `raykhalit.workers.dev`, existing Worker `asynchronia-telemetry-private-alpha` and unrelated `samuray-tours-clicks`, and **one D1 named `asynchronia-telemetry-private-alpha`**. No separately deployed gameplay Worker or dedicated gameplay D1 found in the inventoried account. Do not reuse telemetry Worker/D1; a Workers subdomain existing does not approve hostnames or deployment.\n- `gameplay-server/remote-client/config.mjs` intentionally has `API_ORIGIN=\"\"` / approval false. `build.mjs` fails closed without an explicitly approved exact HTTPS API origin. `wrangler.api-local-test.jsonc` has a synthetic loopback-only D1 identifier, no real game service target.\n- **Next independent gate:** owner decision on bounded isolated staging, operator/backup/key custody, retention and invitation procedure; then exact resource/origin approval and isolated restore proof before hosted tests. No cloud create/update/delete/deploy, credentials, user invites, or real Safari/two-device testing performed. Unknown deployed generation remains BLOCKED/STOP.\n- Repository task/memory files still have stale pre-merge pointers; separately authorized owner/scope required before modifying them. Canonical Notion is the cross-chat bootstrap.",
